WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.512 --> 00:00:21.434
Gerald heard the crunching sound of something walking along the gravel path.

2
00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:25.577
An enormous stone dinosaur was lumbering toward him!

3
00:00:25.597 --> 00:00:29.059
"It can't see me," Gerald told himself.

4
00:00:29.079 --> 00:00:30.860
"I'm not afraid."

5
00:00:32.724 --> 00:00:35.886
As the dinosaur passed, Gerald reached out and touched it.

6
00:00:38.748 --> 00:00:42.451
The moving statue turned toward him, but Gerald was suddenly afraid.

7
00:00:43.452 --> 00:00:45.373
He took off and ran toward the castle.

8
00:00:46.294 --> 00:00:48.856
Gerald spotted the open window of the treasure room.

9
00:00:51.457 --> 00:00:55.020
He climbed up to the window, using the vine that clung to the castle.

10
00:00:57.942 --> 00:01:00.604
Once inside the room, he turned and looked outside.

11
00:01:02.108 --> 00:01:06.849
In the moonlight he could see that the goat-boy statue was back underneath the willow tree.

12
00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.050
Nothing moved outdoors.

13
00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.431
"This is very strange.

14
00:01:12.291 --> 00:01:13.151
Maybe I'm dreaming."

15
00:01:14.271 --> 00:01:17.132
He shut the window and removed the key from the door lock.

16
00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:23.094
Outside the treasure room, he locked the door again.

17
00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:30.296
Then he put the key in its hiding place and crept along the corridor.

18
00:01:35.508 --> 00:01:40.312
He wandered through the castle, opening doors and feeling safe because he was invisible.

19
00:01:41.372 --> 00:01:44.154
At last he came to a door with light shining under it.

20
00:01:45.195 --> 00:01:48.517
Gerald hesitated for a moment before flinging open the door.

21
00:01:54.222 --> 00:01:55.923
cried a voice from within the room.

22
00:01:59.105 --> 00:02:02.808
Gerald flattened himself against the wall as a man sprang to the door.

23
00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.877
The man flashed a lantern into the corridor.

24
00:02:05.897 --> 00:02:08.939
"It's all right," the man said.

25
00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:11.380
"It was only the door swinging open."

26
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.401
"Close that door!"

27
00:02:13.822 --> 00:02:14.862
growled another voice.

28
00:02:16.963 --> 00:02:18.344
That was fine with Gerald.

29
00:02:18.784 --> 00:02:19.985
He had already seen enough.

30
00:02:20.945 --> 00:02:24.507
A gang of burglars was taking silver out of two large chests!

31
00:02:25.528 --> 00:02:28.990
They had picked the door's lock and now their tools lay on the floor.

32
00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.251
"Hurry up!"

33
00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:32.652
one burglar said.

34
00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.440
Gerald ran down the corridor.

35
00:02:36.421 --> 00:02:37.201
What should he do?

36
00:02:39.262 --> 00:02:40.262
He hurried outside.

37
00:02:41.082 --> 00:02:44.803
Through a window he saw Mabel and her aunt having a delicious supper.

38
00:02:47.084 --> 00:02:52.265
He took out his notebook and pencil and wrote: You know the room where the silver is?

39
00:02:52.786 --> 00:02:55.366
Burglars have picked the lock and are stealing the silver.

40
00:02:55.846 --> 00:02:57.127
Send a man for the police.

41
00:02:57.727 --> 00:02:59.067
A friend P.S.

42
00:02:59.568 --> 00:03:00.628
This is not a joke.

43
00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.241
Gerald looked hungrily at Mabel's supper.

44
00:03:05.982 --> 00:03:08.364
He tied the note to a rock with his shoelace.

45
00:03:09.364 --> 00:03:11.225
Then he threw the rock through the window.

46
00:03:12.966 --> 00:03:15.568
Mabel and her aunt jumped up, shrieking in surprise.

47
00:03:16.888 --> 00:03:19.650
Mabel picked up the rock, and her aunt read the note.

48
00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:24.533
said the aunt.

49
00:03:24.553 --> 00:03:26.874
"Of course this is a joke."

50
00:03:28.095 --> 00:03:30.336
"Please," wailed Mabel.

51
00:03:31.248 --> 00:03:33.229
"Send for the police like he says."

52
00:03:33.249 --> 00:03:35.750
"Like who says?"

53
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.050
snapped her aunt.

54
00:03:38.011 --> 00:03:40.812
"Whoever wrote the note," moaned Mabel.

55
00:03:41.792 --> 00:03:43.953
Gerald realized he must do something more.

56
00:03:43.973 --> 00:03:50.516
"Send for the police at once," he called out in his manliest voice.

57
00:03:50.536 --> 00:03:53.817
"You'll only blame yourself if you don't."

58
00:03:53.837 --> 00:03:58.699
"Auntie, please wake Bates right away," begged Mabel.

59
00:03:58.719 --> 00:04:00.820
"Oh, all right."

60
00:04:01.692 --> 00:04:04.913
Mabel's aunt finally went off to get one of the male servants.

61
00:04:06.293 --> 00:04:08.294
Bates was not happy to be woken up.

62
00:04:10.034 --> 00:04:13.535
But after reading the note, he went to the police on his bicycle.

63
00:04:14.536 --> 00:04:18.857
By the time the police arrived, the burglars and the silver were gone.

64
00:04:19.977 --> 00:04:21.498
Gerald had a long night.

65
00:04:23.178 --> 00:04:27.359
It was late when he crept into bed, exhausted and cold as stone.

66
00:04:32.936 --> 00:04:36.019
The next morning Eliza the maid went into Gerald's room.

67
00:04:36.039 --> 00:04:38.501
"Wake up!

68
00:04:38.821 --> 00:04:40.062
It's a beautiful day!"

69
00:04:45.286 --> 00:04:48.849
She opened the curtains at one window and turned to call him again.

70
00:04:50.911 --> 00:04:52.152
But his bed was empty.

71
00:04:52.172 --> 00:04:54.754
"I wonder where he is."

72
00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.676
She opened the curtains at the other window.

73
00:04:58.577 --> 00:05:01.480
But this time when she turned around, she screamed.

74
00:05:03.589 --> 00:05:05.118
Gerald was lying in the bed!
